# io_uring reader-pool backend — PATCH SKETCH (does not apply as-is)
#
# Target: src/glm53_generate.cu @ current HEAD of glm53-dflash2-4070ti-super
# Env gate: INSIGNIA_GLM53_IO_URING=1 enables, INSIGNIA_GLM53_IO_URING_DEPTH
# (default 64). Default behavior (env unset) is byte-identical to today.
#
# Design: keep the entire window/LRU/priority machinery untouched. In uring
# mode drive 0's reader THREADS are replaced by ONE submitter/reaper thread
# that owns a raw-syscall io_uring ring (no liburing dependency, no SQPOLL,
# fixed files, depth 64). The ring READs land either directly in the 4 KiB
# aligned pinned window (compact-store path, same geometry as
# ShardedIndex::read_span_direct_window) or in a per-SLOT scratch (packed
# sidecar path, one scratch per depth slot instead of per thread). Existing
# pool threads survive as EXPAND workers: they drain a new expand_queue_ of
# windows whose bytes have landed and run the CPU half of stage_packed
# (memcpy bodies + AVX2 scale expand). demand > prefetch priority and
# promote_read() keep working because submission still goes through the
# same deques.
#
# Open items marked TODO (tail-of-shard buffered fallback, PAGECACHE_L2
# interplay, ALT-drive mixed mode) — see bench plan before finishing these.
#
# Expected (to be confirmed by scratch/reader-pool/bench_reader_pool.sh on
# glm-box): +0.0..0.35 GB/s device side (5.5 -> 5.8-5.9 fio ceiling chase),
# i.e. -1..4% ms/token on I/O-saturated phases; possibly nothing. The
# microbench must show io_uring >= pread at bs~13m before this lands.

